<title>USA: APL to expand shipping to Latin America - WSJ.</title>
<headline>APL to expand shipping to Latin America - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipping line APL Ltd  plans to launch service between Houston and various Latin American ports, the Wall Street Journal reported, citing people close to the matter.</p>
<p>The paper's electronic edition said APL -- the U.S.'s second-biggest shipping line -- is making the move to try and capture a share of the $100 billion in annual trade through Gulf Coast ports.</p>
<p>The new shipping service will run from Houston to two Mexican ports, as well as Venezuela, Panama and Colombia, the paper said.</p>
<p>The move will be a direct challenge to CSX's SeaLand Service unit and other shipping lines, the paper said.</p>
